"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2974,"**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya with an uncommon narration. He said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, saying: I read to Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who narrated to me: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to me, on the authority of Abu az-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir (RA), that:

The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he returned from the Umrah of al-Ji'ranah, sent Abu Bakr (RA) to lead the Hajj. We set out with him until we were at al-'Arj, where he called the dawn prayer. When he stood to say the takbir, he heard the sound of camels behind him, so he stopped from saying the takbir. He then mentioned the hadith at length.

He said: When the first day of departure (the 12th of Dhu al-Hijjah) came, Abu Bakr (RA) stood and delivered a sermon to the people, instructing them on how to depart and how to stone the Jamarat, teaching them the remaining rites of Hajj. When he finished, Ali (RA) stood and recited Surah Bara'ah (at-Tawbah) to the people until he completed it."
